  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Tomi tilts her head, the motion sharp and birdlike, and a quick grin pulls at one corner of her mouth. That was way more careful than she expected—like he'd rehearsed the offer in his head and then bolted every door at once. Not coaching, not assuming, just a single stopwatch and her rules. The restraint is almost funny, and it makes her curious in a way she doesn't plan to hand over. She rocks back on her heels once, fast, as if the energy needs somewhere to go.\n\n\"You know what, for one loop with me setting every cue? That could actually be useful. I'm not saying yes to a standing thing or putting you on retainer—don't get excited.\" Her voice is quick and casual, the words almost thrown away, but her eyes stay sharp on his face. She doesn't look away while she says it, like she's watching to see if he really meant all those little doors he bolted.",
